[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-lei-* official-website enrichment (site.journal.edn)" "scripts/lei-site-enrich.cljs"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-lei-site-enrichment", :adr/related ["adr-2607110300" "adr-2607113500" "adr-2607182400"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607182500-cloud-itonami-lei-site-enrichment", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR-2607182500: cloud-itonami-lei-* -- real official-website enrichment (title/description/reachability) per LEI\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"\u307e\u305a\u306f\u516c\u958b\u4f01\u696d\u3092\u5bfe\u8c61\u3067\u826f\u3044\u306e\u3067, lei \u3054\u3068\u306b\u516c\u5f0f\u30b5\u30a4\u30c8\u306a\u3069\u306e\u60c5\u5831\u3092\u53d6\u5f97\u3057\u3066 edn \u306b\u7d44\u307f\u8fbc\u3093\u3067\\\")\n**Scope**: `scripts/lei-site-enrich.cljs` (new, superproject) + `80-data/public/site.journal.edn` in each `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI>` archive repo (ADR-2607110300).\n\n## Context\n\nThe 109 `cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI>` repos already hold a real GLEIF-verified LEI + `:company/website` per public company (`blueprint.edn`) and an archived Terms-of-Use text with provenance (`80-data/public/tos.journal.edn`). The owner asked to fetch official-site info per LEI and fold it into EDN, scoped explicitly to these already-registered public companies (no new discovery/collection step needed -- distinct from the MHLW/Common Crawl discovery-path work, ADR-2607182300/2400).\n\n## Decision\n\nAdded `scripts/lei-site-enrich.cljs` (nbb, per this repo's script-host mandate): for each `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repo (enumerated via `gh api orgs/cloud-itonami/repos`, REST not GraphQL, same rate-limit-friendly choice `kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs` already made), reads `blueprint.edn`'s `:company/website`, does a real `curl` GET against the real official site, extracts `<title>`/`<meta name=\\\"description\\\">`, and appends the result as a new `80-data/public/site.journal.edn` -- the SAME Datomic-style `[entity attr value tx :add]` quad-log format `tos.journal.edn` already uses (no new schema convention invented). A fetch failure/timeout/non-200 is recorded honestly (`:site/http-status`, `:site/fetch-error`), never silently skipped or faked as success. Idempotent-per-day (skips a repo already checked today, re-checking on a later run appends a fresh observation rather than overwriting -- matching the append-only journal discipline).\n\nCommitted directly to each repo's `main` (no feature-branch/PR per repo) -- these are simple read-only archive repos (no CI, no governed actor logic), and the original `tos.journal.edn` data itself landed the same way (`git log`: one direct \\\"Initial archive\\\" commit per repo, verified before choosing this path).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Prototyped the fetch+extract logic against a real official site (wabteccorp.com) before writing the script.\n- Dry-run (`--limit 3 --dry-run`) confirmed correct output with zero writes.\n- Real run (`--limit 3`) pushed real commits to 3 real repos; fetched each back via `gh api .../contents/...` and confirmed the committed EDN parses cleanly and contains the real title/description/status captured live.\n- Idempotent-per-day guard verified: re-running against the same 3 repos correctly SKIPs them (\\\"already checked today\\\") rather than re-fetching or duplicating.\n- Full batch (remaining ~106 repos) launched in background; final counts/failures to be reported once complete (see run log).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Each `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repo gains a second, independently-sourced real-data journal (site reachability/title/description) alongside its existing ToS archive -- both real, provenance-tracked, never fabricated.\n- Re-running this script periodically (not scheduled here, a manual/future-automation decision) keeps `site.journal.edn` a real observation history, not a point-in-time snapshot.\n- Scope stayed exactly to the 109 already-registered public companies the owner named -- no new company discovery/collection was performed.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-18", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607182500: cloud-itonami-lei-* real official-website enrichment (title/description/reachability) per LEI", :adr/source-format "edn"}]